Subject: [PATCH] compulab: dts: Initialize third SuperSpeed host PHY

The Edge-AI USB port patch enables the usb3-2 padctl port and lane, but
the host controller still references only usb3-0 and usb3-1. The Tegra
XUSB driver acquires PHYs by name and treats missing PHYs as optional,
so it can register the SuperSpeed root hub without initializing usb3-2.

Add usb3-2 to both host PHY properties so Linux initializes the third
SuperSpeed lane instead of depending on firmware initialization.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CompuLab Edge-AI carrier configuration]
---
 .../nvidia/t23x/nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hardware/nvidia/t23x/nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi b/hardware/nvidia/t23x/nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi
--- a/hardware/nvidia/t23x/nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi
+++ b/hardware/nvidia/t23x/nv-public/tegra234-p3768-0000+p3767.dtsi
@@ -152,9 +152,10 @@
 			       <&{/bus@0/padctl@3520000/pads/usb2/lanes/usb2-1}>,
 			       <&{/bus@0/padctl@3520000/pads/usb2/lanes/usb2-2}>,
 			       <&{/bus@0/padctl@3520000/pads/usb3/lanes/usb3-0}>,
-			       <&{/bus@0/padctl@3520000/pads/usb3/lanes/usb3-1}>;
+			       <&{/bus@0/padctl@3520000/pads/usb3/lanes/usb3-1}>,
+			       <&{/bus@0/padctl@3520000/pads/usb3/lanes/usb3-2}>;
 			phy-names = "usb2-0", "usb2-1", "usb2-2", "usb3-0",
-				    "usb3-1";
+				    "usb3-1", "usb3-2";
 		};
 
 		/* C8 - Ethernet */
